  "purpose": "End-to-end accuracy benchmark written the way people actually type: short, chatty, unspaced, slang, typos, English and other languages. Each case lists the official rows (data/jobcode_master.json) a knowledgeable person would accept as correct. Used by scripts/check_employment_benchmark.mjs to measure top-1 / top-3 accuracy and how often the person is stopped by a question before seeing candidates.",
  "important": [
    "Expected codes were looked up by name in data/jobcode_master.json, not typed from memory.",
    "occ / ind list every acceptable code. A code ending in '*' accepts any code with that prefix (e.g. '56*' = any 음식점·주점업 row).",
    "An empty or missing list means that track is not scored for the case (the sentence does not say enough).",
    "This file scores retrieval against the table as shipped. It does not prove the table itself matches the official KSCO8/KSIC11 publication."
